    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.dice_similarity - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.dice_similarity.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.dice_similarity()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Get Dice similarity coefficient between all node pairs.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.dice_similarity()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Get Dice similarity coefficient between all node pairs.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.dice_similarity()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Get Dice similarity coefficient between all node pairs.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nGet Dice similarity coefficient between all node pairs.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L38126-L38221){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.dice_similarity()\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Dice similarity](../assets/graphs/dice-similarity.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Nodes B and E are outlined in the accent color with their shared neighbors C and D filled in accent. The card doubles the 2 shared neighbors to 4 and divides by the summed degrees 3 + 4 = 7: Dice similarity 0.571.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nThe Dice coefficient measures similarity between two nodes based on their neighborhood\noverlap:\n\n`Dice(A, B) = 2 × |neighbors(A) ∩ neighbors(B)| / (|neighbors(A)| + |neighbors(B)|)`\n\nRange: `[0, 1]` where `0` means no common neighbors and `1` means identical neighborhoods\n(or same node). Self-similarity is always `1.0`.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [dict[int, dict[int, float]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Nested dictionary mapping node IDs to dictionaries of similarity scores. Format:\n    `{node1_id: {node2_id: similarity_score}}`.\n:::\n\n## Common Use Cases {.doc-common-use-cases}\n\n- link prediction (similar nodes likely to connect)\n- community detection (nodes with similar neighborhoods)\n- recommendation systems (find similar users/items)\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~jaccard_similarity`) \n\n:   Shared neighbors over all neighbors, which ranks pairs the same.\n\n[](`~overlap_similarity`) \n\n:   Shared neighbors over the smaller neighborhood.\n\n[](`~pairwise_similarity`) \n\n:   A matrix of scores for chosen nodes.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\n`A` knows `C` and `D`, and `B` knows them and `E`, so the two share 2 of their 2 + 3\nneighbors. The coefficient is twice that share, `4 / 5`:\n\n::: {#78b89f0d .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(\"A\", \"C\"), (\"A\", \"D\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"B\", \"D\"), (\"B\", \"E\")]\n)\nlabel = graph.get_label_from_id\nscores = graph.dice_similarity()[graph.get_id_from_label(\"A\")]\n\ndict(sorted((label(n), s) for n, s in scores.items()))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n{'A': 1.0, 'B': 0.8, 'C': 0.0, 'D': 0.0, 'E': 0.0}\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### The same order as Jaccard\n\n`friends()` links 24 members of two clubs in a made-up town, a chess club and a climbing\nclub, who are friends. Ada has three friends and Dev four, and all three of Ada's are\nDev's. That gives them a Jaccard index of `3 / 4` and a Dice coefficient of `6 / 7`:\n\n::: {#2d5e6414 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nfriends = ec.friends()\nnode = friends.get_id_from_label\nada, dev = node(\"Ada\"), node(\"Dev\")\n\n(\n    friends.jaccard_similarity()[ada][dev],\n    friends.dice_similarity()[ada][dev],\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n(0.75, 0.8571428571428571)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nThe Dice coefficient is $2J / (1 + J)$ for the Jaccard index $J$, which only ever rises\nwith $J$, so the two rank every pair in the same order:\n\n::: {#aac1891d .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\njaccard, dice = friends.jaccard_similarity(), friends.dice_similarity()\n\nsorted(\n    ((u, v) for u in jaccard for v in jaccard[u] if u < v),\n    key=lambda pair: jaccard[pair[0]][pair[1]],\n) == sorted(\n    ((u, v) for u in dice for v in dice[u] if u < v),\n    key=lambda pair: dice[pair[0]][pair[1]],\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```\nTrue\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#390ccb94 .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nfriends.plot(\n    highlight={\n        \"accent\": [\"Ada\", \"Dev\"],\n        \"soft\": [(person, \"Dev\") for person in\n                 [\"Ben\", \"Cleo\", \"Ella\", \"Femi\"]],\n    },\n    label_by=\"label\", seed=8,\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#3741